WEBVTT

00:00:00.578 --> 00:00:04.321
Why would a firm spend heavily
on research and development?

00:00:04.828 --> 00:00:08.088
Its chief executive might welcome risk.

00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:10.636
Or the industry might
offer an opportunity

00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:13.704
that even a cautious
executive would pursue.

00:00:14.294 --> 00:00:16.415
Now listen to the earnings call.

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:21.931
An executive may talk boldly to impress
investors, while committing very little.

00:00:22.438 --> 00:00:26.650
If both the decision and the words
are open to interpretation,

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.330
what can we learn by
reading them together?

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.262
Figure 1 starts with a choice.

00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:34.284
Which unobserved trait are we measuring?

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:37.375
Here, it is a chief executive’s
willingness to take risks.

00:00:37.844 --> 00:00:39.613
On the words branch, unsupervised

00:00:39.613 --> 00:00:42.503
discovery builds one
catalogue across firms.

00:00:42.503 --> 00:00:46.178
Three language model readers judge
which topics bear on the trait.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.248
On the deeds branch, researchers

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:51.180
choose a theoretically
justified behavioral measure.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.624
Each application specifies
its target and any covariates.

00:00:55.093 --> 00:00:58.308
Step 3 predicts behavior from
the selected narrative features.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:02.131
Predictions for held-out observations
form the synthesized proxy.

00:01:02.131 --> 00:01:04.330
Step 4 evaluates the measure.

00:01:05.508 --> 00:01:08.756
The CEO study used
a saved topic catalogue.

00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:12.298
Topic 224 described the Canadian market.

00:01:12.298 --> 00:01:15.171
All three readers initially
voted to exclude it.

00:01:15.694 --> 00:01:19.164
Each reader then reviewed
the same passages independently.

00:01:19.164 --> 00:01:23.477
Two saw the discussion of expansion
as evidence of risk taking.

00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:25.738
One still saw geography.

00:01:25.738 --> 00:01:29.328
Under an unweighted two-out-of-three
rule, the topic stayed in.

00:01:29.328 --> 00:01:31.018
The dissent was preserved.

00:01:31.518 --> 00:01:35.297
Across 12 trials and 354 regular topics,

00:01:35.297 --> 00:01:39.591
descriptors alone yielded
66 to 87 selections.

00:01:39.591 --> 00:01:44.777
Passage review raised
that range to 313 to 321.

00:01:45.254 --> 00:01:49.405
The prediction study used
the 321 topics from this trial.

00:01:49.405 --> 00:01:52.395
Would human readers agree
on the borderline cases?

00:01:52.395 --> 00:01:54.330
That test remains open.

00:01:55.523 --> 00:01:59.370
Each firm-year had 321
transformed topic densities

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.681
and one overall sentiment measure.

00:02:01.681 --> 00:02:04.924
Prediction used no firm
controls or fixed effects.

00:02:05.415 --> 00:02:08.589
The target was same-year
R&D divided by assets.

00:02:08.589 --> 00:02:12.196
With positive assets,
missing R&D was set to zero.

00:02:12.687 --> 00:02:16.980
That rule supplied 42.7 percent
of the available targets.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.747
Missing disclosure may
differ from true zero.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.771
Five folds kept connected
firms and executives together.

00:02:23.771 --> 00:02:27.783
Each firm received a score from a
model trained on four other folds.

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:31.746
The models scored 29,506 firm-years.

00:02:31.746 --> 00:02:35.823
Cross-fitted R squared
was 0.5351 for Ridge

00:02:35.823 --> 00:02:40.777
and 0.6128 for XGBoost, for
contemporaneous spending.

00:02:41.289 --> 00:02:44.605
Observed minus predicted
behavior gives a signed gap.

00:02:44.605 --> 00:02:46.525
It cannot establish intent.

00:02:46.525 --> 00:02:49.330
The dividend study uses
the prediction itself.

00:02:50.495 --> 00:02:52.834
Does the score relate
to a different decision?

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:55.996
Following the Caliskan and Doukas
dividend-policy setting,

00:02:55.996 --> 00:02:58.736
the study asked whether
the firm paid a dividend.

00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:02.650
It used held-out predicted
R&D divided by assets,

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.678
set negative predictions to zero,

00:03:04.678 --> 00:03:07.095
and expressed the score
in percentage points.

00:03:07.612 --> 00:03:10.583
Look at column eight
with actual R&D controls.

00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:13.352
For each one-point increase
in the XGBoost score,

00:03:13.352 --> 00:03:17.227
the estimated log odds fell by 0.1423.

00:03:17.227 --> 00:03:21.549
The firm-clustered
standard error was 0.0347.

00:03:22.066 --> 00:03:25.804
Higher scores were associated
with lower odds of paying dividends.

00:03:25.804 --> 00:03:30.390
The sign was negative in all sixteen
specifications that included a score.

00:03:30.885 --> 00:03:32.426
The final appendix adds eight

00:03:32.426 --> 00:03:36.859
models with both a narrative
proxy and actual R&D controls.

00:03:36.859 --> 00:03:40.913
The synthesized score remains
negative and significant in all eight.

00:03:40.913 --> 00:03:44.330
These additional results
are reported in Table A13.

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:46.976
Return to Figure 1.

00:03:46.976 --> 00:03:48.942
Convergence asks
whether the score tracks

00:03:48.942 --> 00:03:51.548
both narrative and behavioral measures.

00:03:51.548 --> 00:03:53.480
Checking it against
an independent measure

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.108
of executive risk
preference remains open.

00:03:56.615 --> 00:03:58.461
Suppose an industry shock changes

00:03:58.461 --> 00:04:01.763
both the language of earnings
calls and research spending.

00:04:01.763 --> 00:04:05.065
If industry and firm conditions
account for the association,

00:04:05.065 --> 00:04:07.910
the interpretation as
a personal trait weakens.

00:04:08.395 --> 00:04:11.409
Or shuffle the narrative
features and fit the same models.

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:13.719
If shuffled topics predict just as well,

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:16.484
topic selection has little
claim to the result.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.826
WordDeed provides the results,

00:04:18.826 --> 00:04:21.802
reproduction instructions,
and final appendix.

00:04:21.802 --> 00:04:24.855
The next tests will carry
alternative AI selections through

00:04:24.855 --> 00:04:29.330
prediction and assessment, and examine
shared causes and additional constructs.
